error[V0303]: `shout` may change `greeting`, but inside a closure a name from outside can only be read
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0303_captured_name_to_mut_parameter/main.vr:9:15
  |
6 |     let mut greeting = "hello".to_uppercase();
  |             -------- `greeting` is declared outside the closure
...
9 |         shout(greeting);
  |               ^^^^^^^^ `shout` may change `greeting`, but inside a closure a name from outside can only be read
  |
  = note: change it after the call the closure is given to, or make a new value inside the closure instead
  = note: in Rust terms, the closure borrows `greeting` as a shared reference
